{"title":"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the Cheshire Cat function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed216b3cc2b4c17b055d63480f23e705d703c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{:)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"22\" height=\"28\" /> by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/492109c8d6ca206d5040b67f932ce2c9a5b2bda7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  \\fbox{:)}(x) &amp;= -x \\quad \\text {if } x \\text{ is even and} \\\\ \\fbox{:)}(x) &amp;= x \\quad \\text{ if  }x \\text{ is odd}  \\end{align*}\" width=\"224\" height=\"63\" />\n</p><p>Find the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c3e1ec1d0e159159f9edd2cb162dde84de4b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{:)}(1) + \\fbox{:)}(2) + \\fbox{:)}(3) + \\fbox{:)}(4) + . . .+ \\fbox{:)}(289)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"370\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is evident that we are being asked to find the sum of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a1b59d41f13a42f98890e55cf955d534f504fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2+3-4+...-288+289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"238\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>A straight-forward approach is to find the sum of all the odd numbers from 1 to 289, inclusive, and subtract the sum of all the even numbers from 2 to 288, inclusive. Doing so would give you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b176362dbf14509c53b99fb50423c8b332b0f8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145^2 - (144^2 + 144) = (145 - 144)(145 + 144) - 144 = (1)(145 + 144) - 144 = \\boxed{145}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"662\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>However, a faster method would be to see that you can group the terms in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a1b59d41f13a42f98890e55cf955d534f504fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2+3-4+...-288+289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"238\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/87701972b2ebd54a9cf4836d8a6973034c5782a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + (-2 + 3) + (-4 + 5) +...+ (-288 + 289)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"18\" />. Using this, we can reduce many pairs of positive and negative numbers to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s. Since there are as many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s as there are odd numbers between 1 and 289, inclusive, and there are 145 odd numbers, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e3c0459bc205b98a9843145ac15e214e6a4704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)(145) = \\boxed{145}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II\">2014 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017161254\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 108/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1407/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 94/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2120/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.813      1 Template:UNCO_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    7.813      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13477:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017161254 and revision id 113353. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}